course: dictionary
lesson: 6601
title: Nomad: people on the move
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A nomad is a person who moves from place to place instead of living in one place all the time. The sentence gives you clues: «On the wide grasslands of Asia, the Mongols lived as nomads in round felt tents called gers, herding horses, sheep and goats.» Tents you can pack up and animals you herd tell you the people keep moving.
explain: Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Could the Mongols be people who stay in one house? No, because they live in tents they can take with them and they move their herds across the grass. Trying your meaning in the sentence is a good check.
explain: The word also has a looser, everyday meaning. A digital nomad works online while travelling, so they do not stay in one place. Both meanings have the same heart: moving around instead of staying put.
fact: A nomad is a person who moves from place to place with their animals instead of living in one place.
fact: Context clues: tents that can be packed up and animals that are herded show that nomads keep moving.
fact: The steppe is the wide grassland of Asia, where the Mongols lived as nomads.
fact: Informally, a nomad is anyone who moves a lot and has no fixed home.
fact: A digital nomad is someone who works online while travelling.
exercise: «On the wide grasslands of Asia, the Mongols lived as nomads.» What is a nomad? | A person who lives in a castle on a hill | A horse that runs very fast | *A person who moves from place to place instead of living in one place | A tent made of felt
exercise: Find and copy one word from the sentence that names an animal the Mongols herded. | gers | Asia | steppe | *horses
exercise: The Mongols' home is a felt tent that can be packed up and carried. What does this suggest? | They sleep underground | *They can move their home with them | They live in a castle | They never leave the hill
test: Informally, a nomad is anyone who moves a lot and has what? | *No fixed home | A red bicycle | A big garden | A library card
test: Which school subject would teach you about the Mongols, Bedouin and Maasai? | Music | Maths | *Geography and history | Art
exam: Ella's family packed up their felt tent and moved on to fresh grass for their sheep. What does this tell you about nomads? | People who stay in one house forever | People who never keep any animals | People who only live in cities | *People who move with their animals to find grass
